    "description": {
      "chat": "",
      "unidentified": "",
      "value": "<p>On a failed Fortitude save, whenever the subject makes a full attack it gains one extra attack with a held weapon at its full base attack bonus and normal modifiers. This is not an extra action, cannot cast another spell or enable another action, and does not stack with similar extra-attack effects such as <em>bloodlust</em> or a speed weapon.</p><p>The subject takes 1d4 damage each round. One successful save negates the entire spell; the subject cannot accept the extra attack while saving against only the damage. <em>Cripple</em> counters and dispels this spell.</p><p><strong>Automation boundary:</strong> Apply the conditional extra attack and recurring self-damage manually, and enforce non-stacking and the counterspell interaction.</p>"
    },
